    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="1044" n="920" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg920"/>

                <head>No. 563.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Christiancy to Mr.
                    Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-12"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 12, 1881</date>.
                        (Received August 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 330.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you copy and
                    translation of the circular letter of Mr. Galvez, secretary of foreign relations
                    of Peru, dated yesterday, stating the installation of Congress, and the law
                    passed <pb facs="1045" n="921" xml:id="pg921"/> continuing Mr. Calderon as
                    President until the people shall elect another, &amp;c., of which I have
                    acknowledged the receipt.</p>
                <p>A quorum of Congress was obtained, but I think there is room for doubt whether
                    the means adopted to get some of the members here were strictly regular.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>I. P. CHRISTIANCY.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d567-a1.xml" xpointer="d567-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
